abstract: >-
  AgriShield is an open-source parametric micro-insurance platform built on
  Stellar and Soroban. It protects smallholder farmers in Kaduna, Nigeria
  against drought by using automated weather-indexed triggers. When two
  independent oracles agree that rainfall has fallen below a configurable
  threshold, enrolled farmers receive automatic payouts — no claims adjuster
  required. The system comprises a Soroban smart contract (Rust), a Node.js
  oracle service consuming the Open-Meteo API, and a React/TypeScript
  frontend with Freighter wallet integration.
